msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we review how to use PLUMED functionalities for two "
"complementary tasks:"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:67
msgid ""
"Calculating collective variables that capture processes of "
"assembly/disassembly such as the nucleation, condensation, dissolution etc. "
"(Ex. 1, 2)"
msgstr ""

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:69
msgid ""
"Introducing biasing forces through CmuMD, a "
"[method](https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://aip.scitation.org/doi/abs/10.1063/1.4917200__;!!JFdNOqOXpB6UZW0!5LDzfOpI0a0QUEAXjfWbM4f1ubgf4gC-"
"ELH4qKstVB9wJwXRDKOjaCtm52xOb0YEw5vzGbfc4A$ ) that mimics open-boundary "
"conditions and allows for mitigation of finite-size effects. (Ex. 3, 4)"
msgstr ""

